From fb2efcf0923b6ecfcc254e699142ec4e05545038 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:55:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(workers): reuse negative quota probes and coalesce
 metadata receipts [daveey]

Problem: post-load pool boot median remains 6.415s; real Codex trace
spends 1.57s probing an exhausted account and 1.01s in worker-store apply.

Why: quota recovery's five-minute throttle was process-local, so every
fresh worker repeated the same negative HTTPS check. Startup metadata
also fsynced both its pending journal and successful receipt clear.

Keep a 60-second negative-only cross-process throttle scoped to the exact
token, endpoint, reset and failure generation. No positive recovery is
persisted or trusted: absent, invalid and stale records take the live path.
An exhausted account remains exhausted under a memo hit.

Coalesce only same-scope session.prompt/model/sidecars/tools ACK clears
into the next before-send durable pending write. A crash replays the same
sequence/digest through unchanged owner fences. Child, transcript,
compression and terminal receipts still clear synchronously; close flushes.

Detection: new call-count and save-count tests fail on the prior head;
real subprocesses verify negative reuse, and real SQLite verifies crash
windows and fresh-generation refusal. Tests include TTL, home, token,
endpoint and failure/reset separation; positive/unknown results are not shared.

Causal boundary: date/route cohorts show both a shift toward slower Codex
and within-Codex slowdown. PR-merge windows are not controlled deployment
windows and do not prove a PR regression. Preserve original-query natural
post-load >=50-session measurement as the unchanged <=4s acceptance gate.
No forced restarts, routing/pacing changes or weakened persistence fences.
